Nothing particularly major in this update.  The "berserk" thing is at
least partially experimental -- I am going to keep a close watch on its
effects, since I don't really want this to turn into "free conflict!",
and I don't want people's pets to suddenly get constantly splashed in
the early game.  We'll see how it goes, of course.

If anyone knows and can tell me the/a "canonical" term for all the
fantastic monsters Carroll created for his works, I'd appreciate it;
"Carroll beasts" sounds very artificial, but it needed to be something
other than 'jabberwock' to avoid creating messages like "A jabberwock
(invisible snark)".  I seem to remember there being one, but a quick
Google turned up too much garbage to be useful.

List of changes follows:

-------
9/16:
* Bad pun added for land mines
* "Big enough" monsters may attack your pets in order to reach you.
* Some monsters are "berserk" and will attack anything that isn't their 
  own kind between them and you.
* Almost any monster will step on insects in the way.
* Berserk monsters do extra damage when fighting you.  
-- Some low-level monsters' base damage has been downgraded to avoid 
   wrecking the early game with the extra damage
* Purple worm digestion damage upgraded
* "big q" sizes upgraded from LARGE to HUGE
* Ordinary demon speeds all upgraded to at least 9 (aka 'somewhat meaningful')
* Juiblex and Geryon upgraded to speed 6 (aka 'get to move occasionally')

9/12:
* Bug fix: 'J' are now "Carroll beasts", not "jabberwocks".
* Bug fix: Can't ride snarks or boojum anymore

